# =============================================================================
# IMPORTANT
# =============================================================================
# Never commit credentials, passwords, API keys, access tokens,
# private keys, secret environment files, database dumps containing
# sensitive information, or other private/internal security material.
#
# .gitignore is NOT a security boundary.
#
# Sensitive information that has already been committed remains in Git
# history even after adding it to this file. Compromised credentials must
# be revoked/rotated and repository history handled appropriately.
#
# Review files before every commit:
#
# git status
# git diff --staged
#
# Project documentation, source code, Makefiles, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
# go.mod, go.sum, Debian packaging configuration, and other intentional
# source-controlled files should remain tracked.
